      "description": "Learn it. Wire it. Energize it. Check your work.\n\nBuilt by a working journeyman lineman for linemen and their apprentices. The XFMR Lab simulates distribution transformer banks driven by your own wiring — the metering, fusing, and faulting all behave the way you'd expect in the field.\n\nNEW IN 2.0 — BUILT-IN TRANSFORMER TRAINING (Replacing XFMR INFO)\n\nSix guided lessons take you from \"what's a transformer?\" to wiring a 3-pot bank:\n• Start Here — What is a Transformer?\n• Dual H Bushings — The Two Wirings & the Nameplate\n• The Tap Changer — One Pot, Multiple System Voltages\n• Three-Phase — The Three Phases and How They're Related\n• Bank Identification — Delta or Wye, Open or Closed\n• Your First Bank: Delta-Wye Closed (120/208)\n• More lessons on the way!\n\nWork the lessons in order, or jump straight to the labs.\n\nALSO NEW IN 2.0\n\n• The Sandbox (Beta) — wire anything from scratch in a COMPLETELY-customizable lab, with live, vector-based voltage and fault logic baked in.\n• Death Traps — scenario-based transformer traps linemen run into — and how to navigate them safely.\n• A brand-new look across every lab — new graphics, sharper, faster, & easier to read in the field.\n• Voltmeter you can now drag with two fingers; readings update as the leads move.\n• Parallel the secondary coils by hand in wye secondary labs\n• Stats that track lab completions, quiz scoring and for-fun stuff like the number of fuses you've blown.\n• User Customizations - the user can now alter the spec of their labs; from grounding to parallel coil cutover-direction, requiring the 4th cutout, tap changer implementation and more.\n• 2.0 is FREE for everyone who already owns XFMR Lab — thank you for years of feedback and encouragement.\n\nWHAT YOU GET\n\nSingle Phase — Single Bushing · Dual Bushing\nThree Phase (closed) — Delta-Delta · Delta-Wye · Wye-Delta · Wye-Wye\nThree Phase (open) — Open Delta-Delta · Open Wye-Delta\nMisc — Paralleling · 4th Cutout · Death Traps (6 Scenarios)\nAdvanced — Straight 480 · 240/480 · 277/480 · Corner-Grounded 240/480 · Wye-Wye 5-Wire (120/240 + 120/208) - all now able to be wired up Wye AND Delta on the topside\nThe Sandbox (Beta)\nEVERY FUTURE UPDATE IS FREE - THE APP IS A ONE-TIME PURCHASE. I'm always working on new updates.\n\nTOOLS & REFERENCE\n\n• Volt, ohm and rotation meters with real behavior\n• Nameplate, secondary coil and tap changer animations\n• Reference diagrams for every standard bank\n\nLearning Mode walks apprentices through every wrong-connection check. Journeymen and experienced users can keep this turned off if they'd like.\n\nQUIZZES\n\n• Classic Quiz — Select each lab you want in your quiz - with graded scoring across each lab.\n• Advanced Quiz — You're provided with the job-site info and need to pick the right nameplate and coil setup, then wire it.\n• Bank ID - A beginner's quiz tied into the new XFMR Training lesson plan. The user is provided with different primary and secondary wirings and must correctly identify them.\n\nUsed by 30,000+ linemen since 2021.\n\nQuestions? Suggestions? Reach me at info@digitalapprentice.net",
